.TH "TIR" "1" "2026" "tir v0.8" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tir \- kitchen timer with notification, speech, and countdown
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]tir\f[R] [\f[I]options\f[R]] [\f[I]wait\f[R]] [\f[I]what\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]tir\f[R] is a command line kitchen timer for Apple macOS 10.9
(Mavericks) and later.
It will show the message on terminal, notification center, and read it
out using audible speech.
The default message is \(lqTea is ready\(rq and the \(lqtea\(rq is
replaced by the command argument.
If the first argument is a number, the command waits that time in
seconds.
.PP
Time can be specified with suffixes: \f[B]60\f[R] (seconds),
\f[B]3min\f[R] (minutes), \f[B]1h\f[R] (hours), or \f[B]5:30\f[R]
(minutes:seconds).
.PP
Countdown messages are announced every 10 minutes (>10min), every minute
(>1min), then at 30, 20, 10, and 5 seconds.
Use the \f[B]\-c\f[R] option to set a fixed interval, or 0 to disable.
.PP
If Music is playing, its volume is faded to half by default during a
speech.
Select control from \f[I]fade\f[R], \f[I]volume\f[R], \f[I]pause\f[R] or
\f[I]no\f[R] by the \f[B]\-i\f[R] option.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\-w\f[R] \f[I]time\f[R]
Wait time (default: 0).
.TP
\f[B]\-m\f[R] \f[I]message\f[R]
Set message format (default: \(lq%s is ready\(rq).
.TP
\f[B]\-c\f[R] \f[I]time\f[R]
Set countdown interval (default: adaptive, set 0 to disable).
.TP
\f[B]\-C\f[R] \f[I]count\f[R]
Set message repeat count (default: 1).
.TP
\f[B]\-I\f[R] \f[I]time\f[R]
Set message repeat interval in seconds (default: 2).
.TP
\f[B]\-v\f[R] \f[I]voice\f[R]
Choose speech voice (default: Fred).
Use \f[B]\-v ?\f[R] to list available voices.
.TP
\f[B]\-r\f[R]
Same as \f[B]\-v random\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-l\f[R] \f[I]voice\f[R]
Choose voice for last message.
.TP
\f[B]\-b\f[R] \f[I]sound\f[R]
Choose notification sound (default: Default).
Use \f[B]\-b ?\f[R] to list available sounds.
.TP
\f[B]\-V\f[R] \f[I]volume\f[R]
Set system sound volume temporarily (0\-100).
Volume is restored after one second.
.TP
\f[B]\-i\f[R] \f[I]control\f[R]
Music control during speech: \f[I]fade\f[R] (default), \f[I]volume\f[R],
\f[I]pause\f[R] or \f[I]no\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-W\f[R] \f[I]count\f[R]
Set syllable count manually for \f[B]\-G\f[R] option.
.TP
\f[B]\-e\f[R]/\f[B]\-E\f[R]
Echo message or not (default: yes).
.TP
\f[B]\-n\f[R]/\f[B]\-N\f[R]
Send notification or not (default: yes on macOS).
.TP
\f[B]\-s\f[R]/\f[B]\-S\f[R]
Speak or not (default: yes on macOS).
.TP
\f[B]\-R\f[R]
Ramen shortcut (3 minutes).
.TP
\f[B]\-Y\f[R]
Yakisoba shortcut (4 minutes).
.TP
\f[B]\-U\f[R]
Udon shortcut (5 minutes).
.TP
\f[B]\-GR\f[R], \f[B]\-GY\f[R], \f[B]\-GU\f[R]
Gorgeous versions of \f[B]\-R\f[R], \f[B]\-Y\f[R] and \f[B]\-U\f[R].
These use the \(lqGood News\(rq voice to sing the completion message to
a melody.
The message format is automatically adjusted based on the syllable count
of the target word to match the melody timing.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\f[B]tir 60\f[R]
Wait 60 seconds and say \(lqTea is ready\(rq.
.TP
\f[B]tir 180 Ramen\f[R]
Wait 180 seconds and say \(lqRamen is ready\(rq.
.TP
\f[B]tir 5min Your noodle\f[R]
Wait 5 minutes and say \(lqYour noodle is ready\(rq.
.TP
\f[B]tir \-c 10 10min\f[R]
Wait 10 minutes with countdown every 10 seconds.
.TP
\f[B]tir \-GR\f[R]
Gorgeous ramen timer (3 minutes with Good News voice).
.SH TIPS
Apple removed the voice \(lqGood News\(rq, used by the \f[B]\-G\f[R]
option, from the default voice list on recent operating systems.
You can download it from System Preferences: select Accessibility, then
Speech, and choose Customize in the System Voice pulldown.
.SH BUGS
When used with the \f[B]\-G\f[R] option, the command counts syllables
using a very simple algorithm, which sometimes produces incorrect
results.
Use the \f[B]\-W\f[R] option to manually specify the correct syllable
count.
.SH SEE ALSO
osascript(1), say(1)
